{{!
    @template mod_aibranchedscenario/node

    One decision point in the scenario.

    Classes required for JS:
    * aibs-choice

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-action="choose"
    * data-choiceid

    Context variables required for this template:
    * id string Node identifier
    * title string Short node title
    * stage int Narrative stage number
    * situationparas string Situation, array of plain-text paragraphs
    * speech string What a character says, plain text
    * challenge string The direct question put to the learner
    * challengeisquestion bool Whether that line already reads as a question
    * askwhatyoudo bool Whether the player supplies the question itself
    * speaker string Who says the speech line, or empty
    * speakerinitial string First letter of that name, for the avatar
    * hasspeaker bool Whether a named person says the line
    * hasspeechaudio bool Whether that line has a recording to play
    * crisis bool Whether the crisis variant is showing
    * imageurl string Scene image URL, or empty
    * imagealt string Scene image alternative text
    * hasimage bool Whether an image is present
    * hasspots bool Whether the options can be pointed at in the picture
    * marks array Tags pinned to the picture for what this learner did earlier
    * hasmarks bool Whether there are any
    * hasartefact bool Whether a workplace document is in their hands
    * artefact object That document, see mod_aibranchedscenario/artefact
    * askconfidence bool Whether to offer the "not sure" tick
    * choices array The available choices

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": "n2",
        "title": "The fault nobody logged",
        "stage": 2,
        "situationparas": ["Sam lowers his voice."],
        "speech": "Can't we just fix it ourselves?",
        "challenge": "What do you say to Sam?",
        "challengeisquestion": true,
        "askwhatyoudo": false,
        "speaker": "Sam",
        "speakerinitial": "S",
        "hasspeaker": true,
        "hasspeechaudio": true,
        "crisis": false,
        "imageurl": "",
        "imagealt": "",
        "hasimage": false,
        "hasspots": false,
        "marks": [],
        "hasmarks": false,
        "hasartefact": false,
        "artefact": {"kind": "", "kindlabel": "", "title": "", "subtitle": "",
            "fields": [], "hasfields": false, "lines": [], "haslines": false, "footer": ""},
        "askconfidence": true,
        "choices": [{"id": "n2_a", "letter": "A", "text": "Log the fault now and tell the supervisor."}]
    }
}}
<article class="aibs-card aibs-node aibs-slide aibs-enter {{^hasimage}}aibs-noscene{{/hasimage}}"
         data-nodeid="{{id}}" data-stage="{{stage}}">

    {{#hasimage}}
        <div class="aibs-scene">
            <img src="{{imageurl}}" alt="{{imagealt}}" class="aibs-scene-img" loading="lazy">
            {{#hasspeaker}}
                <span class="aibs-speaker">
                    {{#hasspeechaudio}}
                        <button type="button" class="aibs-avatar aibs-is-unplayed" data-action="speak"
                                title="{{#str}} listento, mod_aibranchedscenario, {{speaker}} {{/str}}"
                                aria-label="{{#str}} listento, mod_aibranchedscenario, {{speaker}} {{/str}}">
                            <span class="aibs-avatar-initial" aria-hidden="true">{{speakerinitial}}</span>
                            <svg class="aibs-icon aibs-avatar-play" viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                 aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                                <path d="M7.4 5.6 14.2 10l-6.8 4.4Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                            </svg>
                        </button>
                    {{/hasspeechaudio}}
                    {{^hasspeechaudio}}
                        <span class="aibs-avatar aibs-is-silent">
                            <span class="aibs-avatar-initial" aria-hidden="true">{{speakerinitial}}</span>
                        </span>
                    {{/hasspeechaudio}}
                    <span class="aibs-speaker-name">{{speaker}}</span>
                    {{#hasspeechaudio}}
                        <span class="aibs-speaker-hint">
                            {{#str}} listento, mod_aibranchedscenario, {{speaker}} {{/str}}</span>
                    {{/hasspeechaudio}}
                </span>
            {{/hasspeaker}}

            {{! SPOT IT. When the options are things you can point at, the scene becomes the
                question: look around, find what matters, and answer by pointing at it.
                Teaching somebody to notice is not the same as asking them which of three
                sentences is the hazard, and this is the only way the product can tell the
                difference.

                Deliberately AN ADDITIONAL WAY TO ANSWER, never the only one. The lettered
                options are still below, still keyboard reachable, still read by a screen
                reader - so nothing here is the sole route to a decision, and a learner who
                cannot use a pointer loses nothing but the picture. Each region is a real
                button with the option's own words on it, so it is announced properly
                rather than as an unlabelled box. }}
            {{#hasspots}}
                <div class="aibs-spots" data-region="spots">
                    {{#choices}}
                        {{#hashotspot}}
                        <button type="button" class="aibs-spot" data-action="choose"
                                data-choiceid="{{id}}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"
                                style="left:{{spotx}}%;top:{{spoty}}%;width:{{spotw}}%;height:{{spoth}}%"
                                title="{{text}}">
                            <span class="aibs-spot-ring" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="aibs-visually-hidden">{{text}}</span>
                        </button>
                        {{/hashotspot}}
                    {{/choices}}
                </div>
            {{/hasspots}}

            {{! THE ENVIRONMENT REMEMBERING. A tag pinned to the frame for something this
                learner did earlier - the machine they locked out, the guard they left off.
                Only the marks they have actually earned reach the browser, so the picture
                cannot leak what the next decision is about. Drawn rather than generated,
                which is why it is legible on a phone and costs nothing. }}
            {{#hasmarks}}
                <ul class="aibs-marks">
                    {{#marks}}
                        <li class="aibs-mark aibs-mark-{{tone}}" style="left:{{x}}%;top:{{y}}%">
                            <span class="aibs-mark-label">{{label}}</span>
                        </li>
                    {{/marks}}
                </ul>
            {{/hasmarks}}
        </div>
    {{/hasimage}}

    <div class="aibs-node-body">
        <div class="aibs-node-head">
            <span class="aibs-chip">{{#str}} stagenumber, mod_aibranchedscenario, {{stage}} {{/str}}</span>
            {{#crisis}}
                <span class="aibs-chip aibs-chip-alert">
                    <svg class="aibs-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <path d="M10 2.6 18.4 17H1.6L10 2.6Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                        <path d="M10 7.8v4.1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                        <circle cx="10" cy="14.4" r="0.95" fill="currentColor"/>
                    </svg>
                    {{#str}} tensionhigh, mod_aibranchedscenario {{/str}}
                </span>
            {{/crisis}}
        </div>

        {{#title}}<h3 class="aibs-h3">{{title}}</h3>{{/title}}

        <div class="aibs-prose">{{#situationparas}}<p>{{.}}</p>{{/situationparas}}</div>

        {{! THE DOCUMENT IN THEIR HANDS. Placed after the situation and before the question,
            because that is the order it happens in: you are told what is going on, you pick
            the paper up, then somebody asks you what you want to do. }}
        {{#hasartefact}}
            {{#artefact}}
                {{> mod_aibranchedscenario/artefact }}
            {{/artefact}}
        {{/hasartefact}}

        {{#speech}}
            <blockquote class="aibs-speech">
                <svg class="aibs-icon aibs-speech-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M3 5.4A1.9 1.9 0 0 1 4.9 3.5h10.2A1.9 1.9 0 0 1 17 5.4v6.3a1.9 1.9 0 0 1-1.9 1.9H8.6L4.6 17v-3.4h-.7A1.9 1.9 0 0 1 3 11.7Z"
                          fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                </svg>
                <p class="aibs-speech-text">{{speech}}</p>
            </blockquote>
        {{/speech}}

        {{#challenge}}
            <p class="aibs-challenge {{^challengeisquestion}}aibs-challenge-context{{/challengeisquestion}}">
                {{challenge}}</p>
        {{/challenge}}

        {{#askwhatyoudo}}
            <p class="aibs-challenge aibs-challenge-ask">
                {{#str}} whatdoyoudo, mod_aibranchedscenario {{/str}}</p>
        {{/askwhatyoudo}}

        {{#iscontinue}}
            <div class="aibs-continuewrap">
                {{#choices}}
                    <button type="button" class="aibs-btn aibs-btn-primary aibs-continuebtn"
                            data-action="choose" data-choiceid="{{id}}">
                        <span class="aibs-choice-text">{{text}}</span>
                        <svg class="aibs-icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                            <path d="M4 10h11M11 6l4 4-4 4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                  stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                        </svg>
                    </button>
                {{/choices}}
            </div>
        {{/iscontinue}}

        {{! NOT SURE. One box, volunteered, never required, and read at the moment of the
            click so it is recorded BEFORE the outcome is known - asked afterwards it would
            be a memory of how sure they were, edited by having just been told whether they
            were right.

            The obvious design was to ask on every decision. The obvious design is wrong: it
            puts a second interaction on the one screen the product is built around, and what
            it measures is how willing somebody is to answer a question about themselves. The
            fact a trainer most needs is produced by NOT ticking this - a poor decision taken
            by somebody who was sure is a misconception, not a gap - and producing it costs
            the learner nothing at all. }}
        {{#askconfidence}}
            <p class="aibs-unsure">
                <input type="checkbox" class="aibs-unsure-box" data-region="unsure"
                       id="aibs-unsure-{{id}}">
                <label class="aibs-unsure-label" for="aibs-unsure-{{id}}">
                    {{#str}} notsure, mod_aibranchedscenario {{/str}}</label>
            </p>
        {{/askconfidence}}

        {{^iscontinue}}
        <fieldset class="aibs-choices">
            <legend class="aibs-visually-hidden">{{#str}} choosealegend, mod_aibranchedscenario {{/str}}</legend>
            {{#choices}}
                <button type="button" class="aibs-choice" data-action="choose" data-choiceid="{{id}}">
                    <span class="aibs-choice-letter" aria-hidden="true">{{letter}}</span>
                    <span class="aibs-choice-text">{{text}}</span>
                    <svg class="aibs-icon aibs-choice-arrow" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                        <path d="M4 10h11m-4.4-4.6L15.2 10l-4.6 4.6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                              stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    </svg>
                </button>
            {{/choices}}
        </fieldset>
        {{/iscontinue}}
    </div>
</article>
